Theorem PL-4: Step 10 (realize_annotations, phase 2) follows Step 9 (merge_blocks) — phase 2 uses ArcVarId-keyed lookups surviving merge

  Preconditions:
    - The AIMS pipeline is a 12-step strictly-ordered sequence per
      Annex E §AIMS + arc.md sec-Pipeline. PL-4 fixes ONE intra-
      function step boundary: Step 10 (realize_annotations — phase 2) SHALL
      FOLLOW Step 9 (merge_blocks).
        Step 9: merge_blocks() — CFG cleanup (block renumbering)
        Step 10: realize_annotations() — Phase 2: COW + drop hints (post-merge)
    - PL-4 statement (per Annex E §AIMS PL-4 + arc.md sec-Pipeline
      "realize_annotations() (step 10) must run AFTER merge_blocks() (step
      9) — it accesses AimsStateMap via ArcVarId-keyed lookups
      (var_state_at_block_entry); position-keyed state map fields are stale
      after merge"): realize_annotations SHALL follow merge_blocks, and
      phase 2 SHALL access the state map only through ArcVarId-keyed lookups
      that survive the merge.
    - PL-4 type signature (per Pipeline.proof lines 37-42, the sorry
      obligation this theorem discharges):
        type : Function -> Pipeline
        realize_annotations (Step 10 phase 2) SHALL follow merge_blocks
        (Step 9); phase 2 uses ArcVarId-keyed AimsStateMap lookups surviving
        merge (var_state_at_block_entry).
    - Shipped per-function driver: ori_arc::pipeline::aims_pipeline::
      run_aims_pipeline (compiler/ori_arc/src/pipeline/
      aims_pipeline/mod.rs lines 163-287). The relevant straight-line
      statements:
        (a) Steps 6-9 — `postprocess::verify_and_merge(func, config)?`
            (mod.rs line 275), whose last statement runs Step 9 merge_blocks
            (postprocess.rs line 47).
        (b) Step 10 — `apply_phase_2_annotations(func, &state_map, config,
            &mut result)` (mod.rs line 277), the NEXT statement after
            verify_and_merge, which calls realize_annotations.
      The verify_and_merge call (line 275) completes before
      apply_phase_2_annotations (line 277) begins, so Step 9 precedes Step
      10 unconditionally.
    - Shipped phase-2 wrapper: ori_arc::pipeline::aims_pipeline::
      apply_phase_2_annotations (mod.rs lines 291-333) calls
      crate::aims::realize::realize_annotations(func, state_map, ...) (mod.rs
      lines 299-307). Per realize/mod.rs lines 191-194 this function "Runs
      AFTER merge_blocks() (step 9)".
    - Shipped phase-2 emission: ori_arc::aims::realize::realize_annotations
      (compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/realize/mod.rs lines
      201-209) reads the state map via the ArcVarId-keyed accessor
      var_state_at_block_entry: realize/mod.rs line 310
      (`ctx.state_map.var_state_at_block_entry(blk, var)`) and line 359
      (`ctx.state_map.var_state_at_block_entry(blk, receiver)`). That
      accessor (state_map.rs lines 646-656) is keyed by (ArcBlockId,
      ArcVarId) and the merge pass preserves entry block IDs, so the lookup
      survives merge. Per arc.md sec-Pipeline "The state map is accessed by
      walking the post-merge IR block indices and using those as block IDs
      into the pre-merge state map — this works because merge_blocks()
      preserves entry block IDs."
    - The merge invalidation that PL-4 routes around: AimsStateMap's
      position-keyed block_entry_states / block_exit_states vectors
      (state_map.rs lines 218-227) are indexed by ArcBlockId::index() and
      become stale after merge_blocks renumbers blocks (PL-3). Phase 2
      therefore must NOT read those raw vectors directly post-merge — it
      reads through var_state_at_block_entry, which the merge preserves for
      entry blocks.
    - This theorem reasons over the LINEAR per-function pipeline DAG; PL-4
      is the downstream sibling of PL-3 (Step 5 precedes Step 9) and PL-4a
      (Step 8a precedes Step 9): together they fix the merge boundary —
      phase 1 + unwind cleanup BEFORE merge, phase 2 AFTER merge.

  Soundness property:
    Forall function F processed by run_aims_pipeline.
      Let pos_9 = position(Step 9 merge_blocks on F) and
          pos_10 = position(Step 10 realize_annotations on F)
      in the total intra-function execution order.
      Two conjuncts SHALL hold:

      (P1) Phase-2-after-merge:
        pos_9 < pos_10. merge_blocks completes (the CFG is in its final
        merged shape) strictly before realize_annotations emits COW + drop-
        hint phase-2 annotations.

      (P2) ArcVarId-keyed-survival:
        Every state-map read by phase 2 goes through an ArcVarId-keyed
        accessor (var_state_at_block_entry), NOT a raw position-keyed vector
        index. Because merge_blocks preserves entry block IDs, the
        (ArcBlockId, ArcVarId) lookup resolves correctly on the post-merge
        IR. No phase-2 read touches the merge-invalidated position-keyed
        block_entry_states / block_exit_states vectors directly.

  Proof obligation:
    Two-part constructive discharge corresponding to (P1) and (P2), by
    structural induction over the per-function 12-step pipeline DAG (linear
    chain ... Step 9 -> Step 10 -> Step 11 -> Step 12) + case analysis on
    phase 2's state-map access mode.

    Part (P1) — Phase-2-after-merge (structural induction over the per-
    function step chain):

      Base case — Step 9 (merge_blocks):
        Step 9 is the last statement of verify_and_merge (postprocess.rs
        line 47), reached from run_aims_pipeline's verify_and_merge call
        (mod.rs line 275). Post-condition: the CFG is in final merged shape;
        position-keyed vectors are now stale.

      Inductive step — Step 10 follows the verify_and_merge return:
        apply_phase_2_annotations (mod.rs line 277) is the straight-line
        statement IMMEDIATELY after verify_and_merge (mod.rs line 275). By
        sequential Rust statement evaluation, line 277 executes only after
        line 275 returns Ok (the `?` on line 275 short-circuits on Err, so
        the only path reaching line 277 is the one where Steps 6-9 — merge
        included — completed). Therefore Step 10 starts after Step 9
        finishes.

      Termination — Step 10 (realize_annotations):
        apply_phase_2_annotations calls realize_annotations (mod.rs lines
        299-307). Per its doc (realize/mod.rs lines 191-194) it "Runs AFTER
        merge_blocks() (step 9)". pos_9 < pos_10 holds on every path through
        run_aims_pipeline. (P1) discharged.

    Part (P2) — ArcVarId-keyed-survival (case analysis on phase 2's access
    mode):

      Case ArcVarId-keyed lookup (the only phase-2 access mode):
        realize_annotations reads the state map exclusively through
        var_state_at_block_entry(blk, var) (realize/mod.rs lines 310 + 359).
        That accessor (state_map.rs lines 646-656) keys on (ArcBlockId,
        ArcVarId): it returns SCALAR for scalar/immortal vars, else looks up
        block_entry_states.get(block.index()).and_then(|s| s.get(&var)).
        Because merge_blocks preserves entry block IDs (arc.md sec-Pipeline),
        the post-merge block index used as `blk` still resolves to the
        intended entry-state map. The lookup is sound on the post-merge IR.

      Case raw position-keyed read post-merge (counterfactual — rejected):
        If phase 2 indexed block_entry_states / block_exit_states directly
        by a raw post-merge block position, it would read the stale pre-merge
        vector at a renumbered index (PL-3's invalidation). The shipped
        realize_annotations does NOT do this — it routes every read through
        var_state_at_block_entry. arc.md sec-Pipeline forbids the raw read:
        "Position-keyed state maps (entry_states, exit_states, instr_states)
        are invalid after merge_blocks() — never query them post-merge." The
        verifier rejects any phase-2 access that bypasses the ArcVarId-keyed
        accessor.

    Coverage gate — pipeline-step ordered-pair enumeration:

      The verifier models the shipped per-function schedule as an ordered
      step list and discharges the ordered-pair predicate position(Step 9)
      < position(Step 10) plus the renumbers-blocks attribute on Step 9 and
      the arcvarid-keyed attribute on Step 10. It asserts:
        - Step 9 (merge_blocks) is present with the renumbers-blocks
          attribute.
        - Step 10 (realize_annotations) is present with the
          arcvarid-keyed-lookup attribute.
        - position(Step 9) < position(Step 10) in the total order.
        - Step 10 is the FIRST post-merge step (no step reorders Step 10
          ahead of Step 9).

      Coverage axes:
        Phase-2-after-merge (P1): the (Step 9, Step 10) ordered pair, with
          Step 10 verified to be the immediate post-merge step.
        ArcVarId-keyed-survival (P2): Step 10 verified arcvarid-keyed (no
          raw position-keyed read survives the merge boundary into phase 2).

    Negative-direction witness — phase-2-before-merge rejected:

      Hypothetically scheduling Step 10 (realize_annotations) before Step 9
      (merge_blocks) would have phase 2 emit COW + drop-hint annotations
      against the pre-merge CFG, which merge_blocks then renumbers — the
      annotations' (block_idx, instr_idx) coordinates would become invalid
      exactly as the merge module-doc warns (block_merge/mod.rs lines 39-44:
      drop hints "would become invalid if blocks are renumbered after hint
      computation"). merge_blocks even defensively clears stale drop hints at
      entry (block_merge/mod.rs lines 72-73). The verifier rejects any
      schedule with position(Step 10) <= position(Step 9).

    Negative-direction witness — phase-2 raw-position-keyed read rejected:

      Even with Step 10 after Step 9, a phase-2 read of the raw
      block_entry_states vector by post-merge index would address a
      renumbered (wrong) block. The shipped phase 2 reads only through
      var_state_at_block_entry (realize/mod.rs lines 310 + 359), which is
      merge-safe because merge preserves entry block IDs. The verifier
      rejects any phase-2 access bypassing the ArcVarId-keyed accessor.

    Cycle-soundness witness — PL-4 is the post-merge sibling of PL-3/PL-4a:

      PL-4 fixes the Step-10-after-Step-9 boundary. Its antecedent is PL-3
      (Step 5 phase 1 precedes Step 9; phase-1 position-keyed reads close
      before merge) and PL-4a (Step 8a precedes Step 9; unwind cleanup runs
      before merge). PL-4 completes the merge-boundary triad: phase 1 +
      unwind BEFORE merge, phase 2 AFTER merge via merge-surviving lookups.
      The dependency chain is acyclic:
        PL-3 --> PL-4 (phase 1 before merge implies phase 2 after merge
                      is the only consistent post-merge emission)
        PL-4a --> PL-4 (unwind-edge cleanup before merge keeps the CFG
                      well-formed for phase 2's post-merge walk)
        PL-4 --> PL-5 (no stale summaries — phase 2 reads only the
                      merge-surviving ArcVarId-keyed lookups)
      PL-4 produces nothing PL-3 or PL-4a consumes; no cycle.

    Algorithm-citation declaration:
      property: intra-function pipeline-step ordering (post-merge
                           annotation phase 2 runs after the CFG merge and
                           reads only merge-surviving ArcVarId-keyed state)
      published: standard "recompute-position-free-results-after-
                           CFG-cleanup" discipline — passes that survive
                           block renumbering key on stable value identities
                           rather than block coordinates; matches the
                           value-keyed (vreg) survival of analysis results
                           across LLVM CFG simplification cited in arc.md
                           sec-Reference Repos
      determinism: deterministic — verify_and_merge -> merge_blocks
                           (postprocess.rs line 47) followed by
                           apply_phase_2_annotations -> realize_annotations
                           (mod.rs lines 277 + 299) is a fixed straight-line
                           ordering; no schedule freedom exists
      reference impl: ori_arc::pipeline::aims_pipeline::run_aims_pipeline
                           (mod.rs Steps 6-9 verify_and_merge line 275, Step
                           10 apply_phase_2_annotations line 277) +
                           ori_arc::pipeline::aims_pipeline::
                           apply_phase_2_annotations (mod.rs lines 291-333,
                           realize_annotations call lines 299-307) +
                           ori_arc::aims::realize::realize_annotations
                           (realize/mod.rs lines 201-209, ArcVarId-keyed
                           reads lines 310 + 359) + AimsStateMap::
                           var_state_at_block_entry (state_map.rs lines
                           646-656)

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction (PRIMARY — structural induction over the
        per-function linear pipeline DAG per section_07::
        verify_pl4_annotations_after_merge; the verifier models the shipped
        schedule as an ordered step list and discharges (P1)
        phase-2-after-merge via the ordered-pair predicate position(Step 9)
        < position(Step 10) and (P2) ArcVarId-keyed-survival via the
        renumbers-blocks attribute on Step 9 + the arcvarid-keyed attribute
        on Step 10; emits Fail on any ordering or attribute violation)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — per-case grid over the ArcVarId-keyed-lookup
        case + the rejected raw-position-keyed-read case; gracious-accept
        once structural_induction has discharged the ordering obligation per
        the coverage-manifest PL row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_07 structural_induction engine discharges PL-4 via the per-function pipeline-DAG ordered pair — (P1) Step 10 realize_annotations (phase 2) follows Step 9 merge_blocks (position(Step 9) < position(Step 10): merge_blocks is the last statement of verify_and_merge at mod.rs line 275, and apply_phase_2_annotations -> realize_annotations is the next statement at mod.rs line 277) and (P2) phase 2 reads only merge-surviving ArcVarId-keyed lookups (realize_annotations calls var_state_at_block_entry at realize/mod.rs lines 310 + 359, keyed by (ArcBlockId, ArcVarId) per state_map.rs lines 646-656, sound because merge preserves entry block IDs — never the merge-invalidated position-keyed vectors at state_map.rs lines 218-227); case_analysis secondary-accepting per the coverage-manifest PL row
